# patches/rk3588-topeet/uboot/series — board patches for rk3588-topeet U-Boot
# (mainline u-boot 2026.07-rc4 base, pin 5ca1a73c7d3, evb-rk3588_defconfig).
# One patch filename per line (quilt style); '#' = comment, blank lines OK.
# Applied by scripts/apply-series.sh --component uboot (git am, bisectable).
#
# 0001 — autoboot fix. The stock evb-rk3588 boot_targets (from rockchip-common.h's
# BOOT_TARGETS macro = "mmc1 mmc0 nvme scsi usb pxe dhcp spi") stalls autoboot on
# this board: bootflow hits the pxe/dhcp bootmeths and waits out a BOOTP timeout
# (GMAC PHY autoneg broken, -110/-4) instead of booting the eMMC. Confines
# boot_targets to "mmc0" so bootflow scans only the eMMC bootdev and finds
# /boot/boot.scr on mmc 0:3. Override lives in evb_rk3588.h (BEFORE the
# rk3588_common.h include, so the #ifndef guard in rockchip-common.h adopts it —
# same idiom as genbook-cm5-rk3588.h). See [[rk3588-build-gotchas]] #4.
# 0002 — serial baud. Upstream evb-rk3588_defconfig defaults to 1500000; the
# topeet chain is 115200 end-to-end (DDR ddrbin hack + kernel ttyS2,115200), so
# u-boot at 1500000 prints garbage after BL31 handoff. Force CONFIG_BAUDRATE=115200.

0001-boot-targets-emmc-only.patch
0002-evb-rk3588-baud-115200.patch
# 0003 — autoboot. bootstd's default bootcmd ("bootflow scan -lb") does NOT find
# boot.scr on mmc 0:3 (script bootmeth doesn't match), so autoboot drops to the
# prompt. Bake the known-working manual sequence into CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND:
# load mmc 0:3 ${scriptaddr} /boot/boot.scr; source  (boot.scr then mmc read +
# bootm the raw boot partition). boot_targets (0001) is now moot but harmless.
0003-evb-rk3588-bootcommand-emmc.patch
# 0004/0005 — Loader mode (rockusb), 2026-11-01: mainline implements the vendor
# flash protocol fully; the only thing missing was enabling it. 0004 turns on
# the gadget stack (same 5-line delta as generic-rk3588_defconfig; ums rides
# along) AND sets CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG=0xfd588080 (vendor value) — the
# default 0 compiles setup_boot_mode() into a stub, so the FASTBOOT/UMS
# branches were dead code before this. 0005 pins the OTG dwc3 to the USB2 phy
# (rk3588-generic.dts shape): the combo usbdp PHY has no peripheral mode.
# VID/PID auto-default to 2207:350b (RK3588). Host-side LBA map: wl 64
# idbloader.img, wl 16384 u-boot.itb.
0004-evb-rk3588-rockusb-defconfig.patch
0005-evb-rk3588-otg-peripheral-usb2-phy.patch
# 0006 — 'reboot loader' revival: BOOT_LOADER case in setup_boot_mode() (the
# FASTBOOT/UMS neighbours were already there; LOADER was dropped). Pairs with
# kernel patch 0035 (topeet reboot-mode DT node writing the same register).
# Userspace trigger: reboot(2) RESTART2 "loader" — systemdctl/busybox don't
# pass mode strings, use a raw syscall one-liner (see notes/123).
0006-boot-mode-BOOT_LOADER-rockusb.patch
# 0007 — vol-up Loader entry, 2026-11-02: the maskrom switch is a BROM-level
# strap (E1 board test: no ddrbin banner at all when held), so no firmware can
# intercept it. The board's OTHER vendor entry is the vol-up key — the bottom
# rung (<=17mV) of the SARADC ch1 4-key ladder. Enable the ADC stack and route
# rockchip_dnl_mode_check() to rockusb (mirroring 0006's BOOT_LOADER preboot)
# instead of warm-resetting into BROM download. Key window 30 -> 128: vol-up
# reads ~raw 39 at 1.8V full-scale (30 would clip it); vol-down (417mV ~ raw
# 949) keeps a 7x margin. CONFIG_USE_PREBOOT is the critical ride-along:
# main_loop() never runs preboot without it, so 0006's BOOT_LOADER case has
# been setting a variable nothing executes all along (reboot loader was never
# actually board-confirmed). saradc node shape from rk3588-rock-5b-u-boot.dtsi.
0007-evb-rk3588-adc-volup-loader-key.patch
# 0008 — rockusb PID, 2026-11-02: 0x350b (Kconfig default) is the RK3588 BROM
# maskrom PID, so RKDevTool mislabels our rockusb gadget "MASKROM设备". The
# vendor usbplug that RKDevTool shows as a LOADER device uses 2207:300a
# (descriptor @0x26846 in out/MiniLoaderAll.bin). One-line override.
0008-evb-rk3588-rockusb-pid-300a.patch
# 0009 — bcdUSB classification, 2026-11-02: RKDevTool/upgrade_tool/rkdeveloptool
# classify maskrom-vs-loader by bcdUSB (0x0201 = loader; vendor composite.c
# comment, vendor g_dnl fixup for usb_dnl_rockusb). Mainline composite forces
# 0x0200 on USB2 at descriptor-serve time, so even with PID 0x300a (0008) our
# gadget gets labeled MASKROM. Keep 0x0201 for the rockusb function only.
0009-composite-rockusb-bcdusb-0201.patch
# 0010 — USB2 BOS for rockusb, 2026-11-02: bcdUSB 0x0201 obliges a BOS answer;
# Windows 8+ requests it at enumeration and the stall fails rockusb.sys start
# (STATUS_NO_SUCH_DEVICE / code 10 — board-caught; vendor composite.c carries
# the same workaround). Serve a bare 12-byte USB2-extension BOS (claims
# nothing); also key bos_desc()'s SS cap set on LINK speed —
# gadget_is_superspeed() reflects driver capability, not the HS link.
0010-composite-rockusb-usb2-bos.patch
